-- title:
--   Relative lifting of rigidified curves over Artinian local algebras
-- statement:
--   The setting is the following chain of data.
--
--   **Arithmetic of the base.** Two distinct primes $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hrr : rbar ≠ r`) and a nonzero level $N$ with $r \nmid N$ (`hrN`). A domain $\mathcal{O}$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a field of characteristic zero which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Further, a characteristic-zero domain $O^{nr}$ over $\mathcal{O}$ with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`), such that every $x \in O^{nr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $O^{nr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Quaternionic data.** Rationals $a, b$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and is ramified at exactly the finite places whose ideal contains $r$ or $\bar r$ (`hB`); a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ which is an order maximal among orders (`hΛ`) and contains every rational integer (`hΛℤ`); a map $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{r}^{(2)} \times \mathbb{Z}_{r}^{(2)}$ (values in the Witt vectors of $\mathbb{F}_{r^{2}}$) which, by `hcoord`, is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, satisfies the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule of the definition of `IsOrderCoord`, is injective, has image dense modulo every power of $r$, and matches reduced traces with the sum of the first coordinate and its Frobenius.
--
--   **Reduction data.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ for $(\Lambda, N)$ over $O^{nr}/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over $O^{nr}/(\pi)$ (`hX₀`: the action of $r$ has kernel of degree $r^{4}$), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the structure morphism of $A_0$, and `hA₀`, asserting that $\theta_0$ presents the formal group law of $A_0$ via $X_0$ and intertwines the $\Lambda$-action with the series attached to $\mathrm{coord}$.
--
--   **Special formal module side.** A ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{r}^{(2)} \to O^{nr}$; a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{nr}/(r)$ which is special for the reduction of $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $M$ over $O^{nr}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hM`); and a family $\eta$ assigning to each ring $B$ with a leg $O^{nr} \to B$ in which $r$ is nilpotent a map from rigidified objects `Rigidified r Φ B` to $M$. The hypothesis `hη` has three clauses: over Noetherian $B$, $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to the isomorphism relation `Rigidified.IsIsomorphic`; $\eta$ is natural for ring maps compatible with the legs, applied to admissible objects; and every point of $M$ over Noetherian $B$ is, Zariski-locally on a finite cover of $B$ by principal localisations in which $r$ remains nilpotent and which are Noetherian, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$. Finally $E_0$ is a ring homomorphism from the centraliser of $\{\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}\,a\} \cup \{\Phi.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and `hE₀` asserts that $E_0$ is injective and that for some $m \in \mathbb{N}$ every matrix $A$ over $\mathcal{O}$ occurs as $r^{m}\cdot A$ in the image of $E_0$, while $r^{m} E_0(e)$ always comes from a matrix over $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Transport data.** A ring homomorphism denoted `κ` from $O^{nr}/(\pi)$ to $O^{nr}/(r)$ compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`) — the same two names are reused later for the residue field and its nilpotency hypothesis — together with $n_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ and a pair of power series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along `κ` (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **The comparison map.** $\Xi$ assigns to every Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$, every $\psi : O^{nr} \to_{\mathcal{O}} B$ and every nilpotency witness for the image of $\pi$ in $B$, a map from rigidified curves `RigidifiedCurve r π A₀ B ψ` (a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ together with a rigidification: base changes $E_b$ of $E$ and $A_b$ of $A_0$ over $B/(\pi)$, an integer $d$, and an isogeny pair $\varphi, \varphi'$ of degree $r^{d}$ between them preserving the level structure) to $G$-points of $M$ over $B$ (a leg $O^{nr} \to_{\mathcal{O}} B$, nilpotency of $r$, and a point of $M$). Four hypotheses on $\Xi$ are imposed:
--
--   `hΞleg`: over connected $B$ (every idempotent is $0$ or $1$), the leg of $\Xi(x)$ is $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ for some $k \in \mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   `hΞnat`: for $\varphi : B \to_{\mathcal{O}} B'$, if $x$ over $B$ and $x'$ over $B'$ are compared by a morphism $g$ exhibiting $x'$ as the base change of $x$ along $\varphi$, and the rigidifications correspond under `Rigidification.IsPullbackVia` (equal degrees and on-the-nose compatibility of the isogenies), then $\Xi(x') = \Xi(x).\mathrm{map}\,\varphi$.
--
--   `hΞiso`: for $x, x'$ over the same $(B, \psi)$, an isomorphism $i$ of the underlying curves over $B$ compatible with the group laws, the $\Lambda$-action and the level structures, together with comparisons $i_b$ of the $(\pi)$-reductions (compatible with $g_b$ and the structure morphisms), a comparison $u_A$ of the $A_0$-sides which is a base change along the identity and compatible with $g_A$, and exponents $i_1, j_1$ with $i_b \text{ followed by } \varphi' \text{ followed by } u_A \text{ followed by } [r^{i_1}] = \varphi \text{ followed by } [r^{j_1}]$, forces $\Xi(x) = \Xi(x')$.
--
--   `hΞdef`: over connected Noetherian $B$ with both $\pi$ and $r$ nilpotent, if $x$ has underlying curve presented by a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X$ and coordinates $\theta$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, then there are $j \le 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ over $B$ with $t.X = X$, with $t$ obtained from $(\theta_0, \mathrm{κ}, \beta_0, \theta)$ by the transport relation `IsRigTransport` at level $j$, with $t$ admissible for $\iota$ and the twisted leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$, and $\Xi(x)$ equal to the $G$-point with leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$ and point $\eta(t)$.
--
--   **The Artinian situation.** $A$ is an Artinian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hA`); $\kappa$ is an algebraically closed field over $\mathcal{O}$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent; $q_\kappa : A \to_{\mathcal{O}} \kappa$ is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal of $A$; and $\psi : O^{nr} \to_{\mathcal{O}} A$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every rigidified curve $x_0$ over $\kappa$ with leg $q_\kappa \circ \psi$ and every $G$-point $y$ of $M$ over $A$ whose leg is a Frobenius twist $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ for some $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, and such that $\Xi(x_0) = y.\mathrm{map}\,q_\kappa$, there exist: a rigidified curve $x$ over $A$ with leg $\psi$; a morphism $g$ from the curve of $x_0$ to the curve of $x$ exhibiting the former as the base change of the latter along $q_\kappa$; a morphism $u_b$ from $x_0.2.E_b$ to $x.2.E_b$ exhibiting $x_0.2.E_b$ as the base change of $x.2.E_b$ along the induced map $A/(\pi) \to \kappa/(\pi)$, with $u_b$ followed by $x.2.g_b$ equal to $x_0.2.g_b$ followed by $g$; a morphism $u_A$ from $x_0.2.A_b$ to $x.2.A_b$ exhibiting $x_0.2.A_b$ as the base change of $x.2.A_b$ along the same induced map, with $u_A$ followed by $x.2.g_A$ equal to $x_0.2.g_A$; and natural numbers $i_1, j_1$ such that
--   $$u_b \text{ followed by } x.2.\varphi \text{ followed by } [r^{i_1}] \;=\; x_0.2.\varphi \text{ followed by } u_A \text{ followed by } [r^{j_1}],$$
--   where $[r^{i}]$ denotes the action of the rational integer $r^{i} \in \Lambda$ on $x.2.A_b$, and moreover $\Xi(x) = y$.
--
--   Thus the lift $x$ is required to restrict to $x_0$ only up to multiplication of the rigidifying isogeny by powers of $r$; the degrees $d$ of the two rigidifications need not agree, so the comparison asserted is weaker than the on-the-nose relation `Rigidification.IsPullbackVia` used in `hΞnat`.
--
--   This is the Artinian-level lifting step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison between rigidified fake elliptic curves (with their reductions and rigidifying isogenies to the fixed supersingular curve $A_0$) and points of the moduli package of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules: a point of $M$ over an Artinian local algebra $A$ which is already matched over the residue field is realised by a rigidified curve over $A$ lifting the given one up to $r$-power adjustment. It is used in the proof that the comparison map $\Xi$ is bijective over Artinian local algebras with algebraically closed residue field, and in the corresponding statement with the pull-back and isomorphism comparison data retained.
